.Xr xft 7
.Sh CAVEATS
Every buffer given to a constructor, and
.Fa data Ns .mem
and
.Fa dst Ns .mem ,
must not be
.Dv nullptr ,
and an fs reader's or fs writer's buffer must not be empty; this is assumed,
not checked.
.Pp
On a pipe or terminal,
.Fn xft_reader_stream
and
.Fn xft_reader_read
on an fs reader keep reading until
.Fa limit
or
.Fa dst
is reached or the input ends, so they block until then.
.Pp
After an fs writer fails, the staged bytes are kept even if some were
already written, so flushing again can write them twice.
.Pp
Every read from a growable reader moves the remaining bytes, so its cost
grows with the bytes left.
.Pp
Do not pass the zeroed result of a failed
.Fn xft_map_file_into_memory
to
.Fn xft_unmap_file_from_memory .
